is derived. Permitted Non-Commercial Use includes solely:
  (a) Personal learning, self-study, and non-commercial experimentation;
  (b) Classroom instruction, coursework, student laboratory exercises, and
      non-commercial educational training;
  (c) Student theses, dissertations, and academic degree requirements;
  (d) Independent academic research and university scientific research that is
      genuinely non-commercial and results in open, publicly accessible scholarly
      findings;
  (e) Scientific benchmarking and algorithm comparison not performed for
      commercial benefit or client deliverables;
  (f) Internal non-commercial modifications and adaptations for academic
      laboratory workflows in accordance with Section 4.

CRITICAL NOTICE ON NON-COMMERCIAL ELIGIBILITY: The institutional classification
of an organization (for example, status as an accredited university, college,
school, research institute, hospital, or non-profit entity) does NOT
automatically render every activity conducted within that organization
non-commercial. The legal test is based upon the actual nature, funding, and
purpose of the specific activity. Any research, testing, calculation, or
deployment conducted for commercial clients, sponsored by for-profit entities,
or yielding proprietary commercial work product constitutes Commercial Use.

"Commercial Use" means any use, deployment, or exploitation of the Software
that is not strictly Permitted Non-Commercial Use. Commercial Use includes,
without limitation:
  (a) Internal Corporate Use: Any use within, on behalf of, or for the benefit
      of any for-profit corporation, commercial enterprise, business entity,
      or partnership (including internal research and development, molecular
      screening, drug discovery, or materials design, regardless of whether the
      Software itself is sold or redistributed);
  (b) Commercial Services: Providing paid computing services, calculation
      hosting, batch processing, or time-sharing for commercial customers;
  (c) Hosted SaaS & Cloud Platforms: Operating the Software as a
      Software-as-a-Service (SaaS), cloud service, hosted application, or web
      platform for paying users or as part of a commercial product offering;
  (d) Fee-For-Service & Consulting: Performing contract research, paid
      consulting, fee-for-service calculations, or commercial scientific
      analysis for client deliverables;
  (e) Sponsored Commercial Research: Performing research, computational modeling,
      or calculation workflows funded by, contracted by, or delivering
      proprietary deliverables to a for-profit commercial entity;
  (f) Commercial Integration & OEM: Bundling, embedding, packaging, or
      integrating the Software into any commercial product, hardware appliance,
      or commercial software distribution;
  (g) Commercial Resale & Sublicensing: Reselling, leasing, renting, or
      sublicensing the Software for commercial purposes;
  (h) White-Labeling: Deploying the Software under a white-label, rebranded,
      or commercial proprietary offering.

"Modifications" means any alteration, addition, enhancement, translation, or
